ion is unavailable.\"","\"The predecessor operated since2012; design knowledge and relationships may support repeat business.\"","\"Customer bargaining and replication risks are material; no verified durable pricing, brand or cost advantage.\"","\"Medium\"","\"FY26 revenue8398.45 lakh versus2349.21 lakh is a large nominal increase with no price/volume split.\"","\"FY23 is a partial takeover period; FY26 sales are almost all traded goods and Q1FY27 is much lower than Q4.\"","\"FY24 utilization33.67% suggests physical headroom; the latest quarter grew strongly year on year.\"","\"No defensible three- or five-year underlying comparable growth basis; nominal growth does not justify a starting score 9.\"","\"Gold and diamond demand recurs, and FY24 capacity was substantially unused.\"","\"No binding order book/customer contracts were established; concentration and property funding constrain accessible expansion.\"","\"Domestic jewellery breadth may permit new customers, but no quantified share-capture evidence was established.\"","\"Some accessible runway exists, but unsupported customer conversion/expansion keeps this below the adequate band; returns are assessed separately.\"","\"FY26 equity arithmetic and the share-premium/cash-flow bridge remain inconsistent.\"","\"FY23 BTA added noncash capital, and the new ₹10 crore property lacks incremental unit economics.\"","\"Low utilization could permit incremental sales without much new plant, but working capital still needs funding.\"","\"Additional-capital denominators and normalized earnings are unreliable; diagnostic ROIC is not a scoreable economic return.\"","\"FY25 tax-reclassified CFO25.13 lakh was far below PAT243.28 lakh; FY26 CFO was−2524.19 lakh versus PAT894.67 lakh.\"","\"FY26 closing receivables6489.42 lakh and cash0.94 lakh show collection dependence despite financing; excluding the unexplained positive inflow worsens CFO.\"","\"FY24 generated positive cash, and FY26 reports invoice age under six months; FY23 is excluded from persistent-cash proof due to takeover contamination.\"","\"Repeated weak realization in FY25–26 is not adequately explained as a temporary build; the GQS cap 5 applies, without replacing NS.\"","8","\"March debt1896.13 lakh and cash0.94 lakh contrast with the later ₹10 crore property obligation.\"","\"Remaining warrant exercise is optional; no current cash balance, reliable maturity schedule or committed incremental facility was established.\"","\"Confirmed post-March conversion receipts total ₹5.5068 crore through20October, but that does not prove unused cash.\"","\"Current funding resilience is unscoreable; hypothetical surviving branches do not establish actual solvency.\"","\"Sales grew sharply, but five permanent employees and ₹16 lakh labour revenue leave the manufacturing/trading mix unclear.\"","\"The subsidiary was formed after March; target-versus-delivery and post-property operating milestones are unavailable.\"","\"The prospectus contained physical capacity/product information, and the company continues to report operations.\"","\"No reliable Medium-confidence delivery record exists for the enlarged operating scale.\"","\"PAT rose from243.28 to894.67 lakh, but closing-share-like EPS ignores uneven issuance timing and warrant dilution.\"","\"FY25 company-services expense190.77 lakh materially changed the expense base; normalized recurring margins need explanation.\"","\"FY26 reports no other income, so no explicit asset-sale gain explains reported profit.\"","\"Normalized operating margins, tax and fully diluted per-share earnings are not established; headline PAT growth is not scoreable.\"","\"Entry cash and committed funding remain unverified.\"","\"Every model return depends on declared assumptions for collections, property timing and terminal reinvestment.\"","\"Some illustrative paths survive, but that does not verify their inputs.\"","\"No supported return model or executable en